# Cloudflare Pages routing.
#
# Every static route now ships a real prerendered index.html, and Pages serves a
# matching file before it ever consults this list. So these rules only cover
# what is genuinely dynamic, plus the fallback.
#
# The fallback is the important line. It used to be `/* /index.html 200`, which
# answered EVERY unknown URL with the homepage under a 200 status. To a crawler
# that means "this page exists" — so typos, dead links, and scraped junk URLs
# all become indexable duplicates of the homepage (a soft-404 farm, and a
# duplicate-content problem against the real homepage). Returning a true 404
# keeps them out of the index entirely.

# The /highlights index retired into /projects. Must come BEFORE the wildcard
# below, which would otherwise swallow it into the SPA fallback and answer 200.
/highlights  /projects  301
/Highlights  /projects  301

# Highlight detail pages are addressed by UUID and are rendered client-side.
#
# Rewriting them to `/` instead of `/index.html` matters on Cloudflare Pages:
# `/index.html` is itself redirected to `/`, so using it here can bounce the
# request out of the proxy path entirely.
/highlights/*  /  200
/Highlights/*  /  200

# Admin routes are client-rendered and protected in-app.
/admin  /  200
/admin/*  /  200

# Everything unmatched is genuinely missing.
/*  /404.html  404
